.TH "OPENSC\&.CONF" "5" "06/02/2026" "opensc" "OpenSC File Formats"
.\" -----------------------------------------------------------------
.\" * Define some portability stuff
.\" -----------------------------------------------------------------
.\" ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
.\" http://bugs.debian.org/507673
.\" http://lists.gnu.org/archive/html/groff/2009-02/msg00013.html
.\" ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el       .ds Aq '
.\" -----------------------------------------------------------------
.\" * set default formatting
.\" -----------------------------------------------------------------
.\" disable hyphenation
.nh
.\" disable justification (adjust text to left margin only)
.ad l
.\" -----------------------------------------------------------------
.\" * MAIN CONTENT STARTS HERE *
.\" -----------------------------------------------------------------
.SH "نام (NAME)"
opensc.conf \- configuration file for OpenSC
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.PP
OpenSC obtains configuration data from the following sources in the following order
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04' 1.\h'+01'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP "  1." 4.2
.\}
command\-line options
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04' 2.\h'+01'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP "  2." 4.2
.\}
environment variables
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04' 3.\h'+01'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP "  3." 4.2
.\}
Windows registry key in
HKEY_CURRENT_USER
(if available)
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04' 4.\h'+01'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP "  4." 4.2
.\}
Windows registry key in
HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE
(if available)
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04' 5.\h'+01'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP "  5." 4.2
.\}
system\-wide configuration file (/etc/opensc\&.conf)
.RE
.PP
The configuration file,
opensc\&.conf, is composed of
\fIblock\fRs, which, in general, have the following format:
.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 4
.\}
.nf
\fIkey\fR [,\ \fIname\fR...] {
	\fIblock_contents\fR
}
			
.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
.sp

\fIblock_contents\fR
is one or more
\fIblock_item\fRs where a
\fIblock_item\fR
is one of
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
#
\fIcomment string\fR
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
\fIkey\fR[,\ \fIname\fR...]
=
\fIvalue\fR;
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
\fIblock\fR
.RE
.PP
At the root level,
opensc\&.conf
should contain one or more application specific configuration blocks:
.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 4
.\}
.nf
app \fIapplication\fR {
	\fIblock_contents\fR
}
			
.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
.sp

\fIapplication\fR
specifies one of:
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
\fIfilename\fR: Configuration block for the application with specified file path\&.
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
default: The fall\-back configuration block for all applications
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
opensc\-pkcs11: Configuration block for the PKCS#11 module (opensc\-pkcs11\&.so)
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
onepin\-opensc\-pkcs11: Configuration block for the PKCS#11 one\-PIN\-module (onepin\-opensc\-pkcs11\&.so)
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
cardmod: Configuration block for Windows\*(Aq minidriver (opensc\-minidriver\&.dll)
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
cardos\-tool,
cryptoflex\-tool,
dnie\-tool,
egk\-tool,
eidenv,
gids\-tool,
iasecc\-tool,
netkey\-tool,
npa\-tool,
openpgp\-tool,
opensc\-asn1,
opensc\-explorer,
opensc\-notify,
opensc\-tool,
piv\-tool,
pkcs11\-tool,
pkcs15\-crypt,
pkcs15\-init,
pkcs15\-tool,
sc\-hsm\-tool,
westcos\-tool: Configuration block for OpenSC tools
.RE
.sp
.SH "CONFIGURATION OPTIONS"
.PP
\fBdebug = \fR\fB\fInum\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Amount of debug info to print (Default:
0)\&. A greater value means more debug info\&.
.sp
The environment variable
\fBOPENSC_DEBUG\fR
overwrites this setting\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBdebug_file = \fR\fB\fIfilename\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
The file to which debug output will be written (Default:
stderr)\&. Special values
stdout
and
stderr
are recognized\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBprofile_dir = \fR\fB\fIfilename\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
PKCS#15 initialization/personalization profiles directory for
\fBpkcs15-init\fR(1)
(Default:
/usr/share/opensc)\&.
.sp
If this configuration value is not found on Windows, the registry key
Software\eOpenSC Project\eOpenSC\eProfileDir
is checked\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBdisable_colors = \fR\fB\fIbool\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Disable colors of log messages (Default:
false
if attached to a console,
true
otherwise)\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBdisable_popups = \fR\fB\fIbool\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Disable pop\-ups of built\-in GUI (Default:
false)\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBenable_default_driver = \fR\fB\fIbool\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Enable default card driver (Default:
false)\&. Default card driver is explicitly enabled for
\fBopensc-explorer\fR(1)
and
\fBopensc-tool\fR(1)
.RE
.PP
\fBcard_drivers = \fR\fB\fIname\fR...\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Allowlist of card drivers to load at start\-up\&. The special value
internal
(the default) will load all statically linked drivers\&.
.sp
If an unknown (i\&.e\&. not internal or old) driver is supplied, a separate configuration block has to be written for the driver\&. A special value
old
will load all statically linked drivers that may be removed in the future\&.
.sp
The list of supported card driver names can be retrieved from the output of
\fBopensc\-tool \-\-list\-drivers\fR\&.
.sp
The environment variable
\fBOPENSC_DRIVER\fR
overwrites this setting\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBignored_readers = \fR\fB\fIname\fR...\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
List of readers to ignore (Default: empty)\&. If any of the comma separated strings listed is matched in a reader name (case sensitive, partial matching possible), the reader is ignored by OpenSC\&. Use
\fBopensc\-tool \-\-list\-readers\fR
to see all currently connected readers\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBreader_driver \fR\fB\fIname\fR\fR\fB { \fR\fB\fIblock_contents\fR\fR\fB } \fR
.RS 4
Configuration of the smart card reader driver where
\fIname\fR
is one of:
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
ctapi: See
the section called \(lqConfiguration of CT\-API Readers\(rq
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
pcsc: See
the section called \(lqConfiguration of PC/SC Readers\(rq
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
openct: See
the section called \(lqConfiguration of OpenCT Readers\(rq
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
cryptotokenkit: Configuration block for CryptoTokenKit readers
.RE
.sp
See
the section called \(lqConfiguration of Smart Card Reader Driver\(rq\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBcard_driver \fR\fB\fIname\fR\fR\fB { \fR\fB\fIblock_contents\fR\fR\fB } \fR
.RS 4
Configuration of the card driver where
\fIname\fR
is one of:
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
npa: See
the section called \(lqConfiguration Options for German ID Card\(rq
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
dnie: See
the section called \(lqConfiguration Options for DNIe\(rq
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
edo: See
the section called \(lqConfiguration Options for Polish eID Card\(rq
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
eoi: See
the section called \(lqConfiguration Options for Slovenian eID Card\(rq
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
myeid: See
the section called \(lqConfiguration Options for MyEID Card\(rq
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
dtrust: See
the section called \(lqConfiguration Options for D\-Trust Signature Cards\(rq
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
Any other value: Configuration block for an externally loaded card driver
.RE
.sp
.RE
.PP
\fBcard_atr \fR\fB\fIhexstring\fR\fR\fB { \fR\fB\fIblock_contents\fR\fR\fB } \fR
.RS 4
In addition to the built\-in list of known cards in the card driver, you can configure a new card for the driver using the
\fBcard_atr\fR
block\&.
.sp
For details see
the section called \(lqConfiguration based on ATR\(rq\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBdisable_hw_pkcs1_padding = \fR\fB\fIvalue\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Disabling PKCS#1 v1\&.5 padding in HW when card supports doing raw RSA operations\&. Known parameters:
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
no: PKCS#1 v1\&.5 padding is enabled in HW when card supports it\&.
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
sign: PKCS#1 v1\&.5 padding is disabled only for signatures (PKCS#1 v1\&.5 type 1)\&.
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
decipher: PKCS#1 v1\&.5 padding is disabled only for decryption (PKCS#1 v1\&.5 type 2)\&.
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
both: PKCS#1 v1\&.5 padding is disabled both for signatures and decryption (PKCS#1 v1\&.5 type 1 and 2)\&.
.RE
.sp
(Default:
decipher)\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBopenssl_config = \fR\fB\fIpath\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Specify a OpenSSL configuration file to be loaded into the OpenSC\*(Aqs library context\&. This should not be needed for general operation, but is needed if you need to configure some specifics of OpenSSL, without the need to rebuild OpenSC (for example configure and load a FIPS provider)\&. For more information about configuring OpenSSL, see
\fBconfig\fR(5)
and
\fBfips_config\fR(5)\&. (Default:
empty)\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBsecure_messaging \fR\fB\fIname\fR\fR\fB { \fR\fB\fIblock_contents\fR\fR\fB } \fR
.RS 4
Configuration options for the secure messaging profile
\fIname\fR:
.PP
\fBmodule_name = \fR\fB\fIfilename\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Name of external SM module (Default: libsmm\-local\&.so)\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBmodule_path = \fR\fB\fIfilename\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Directory with external SM module (Default: /usr/lib)\&.
.sp
If this configuration value is not found on Windows, the registry key
Software\eOpenSC Project\eOpenSC\eSmDir
is checked\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBmodule_data = \fR\fB\fIvalue\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Specific data to tune the module initialization\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBmode = \fR\fB\fIvalue\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Secure messaging mode\&. Known parameters:
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
transmit: In this mode the procedure to securize an APDU is called by the OpenSC general APDU transmit procedure\&. In this mode all APDUs, except the ones filtered by the card specific procedure, are securized\&.
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
acl: In this mode APDU are securized only if needed by the ACLs of the command to be executed\&.
.RE
.sp
.RE
.PP
\fBflags = \fR\fB\fIvalue\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Secure messaging type specific flags\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBkmc = \fR\fB\fIhexstring\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Default KMC of the GP Card Manager for the Oberthur\*(Aqs Java cards\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBifd_serial = \fR\fB\fIhexstring\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
.RE
.PP
\fBkeyset[_\fR\fB\fIaid\fR\fR\fB]_\fR\fB\fInum\fR\fR\fB_enc = \fR\fB\fIvalue\fR\fR\fB;\fR \fBkeyset[_\fR\fB\fIaid\fR\fR\fB]_\fR\fB\fInum\fR\fR\fB_mac = \fR\fB\fIvalue\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Keyset values from IAM profiles of the Gemalto IAS/ECC cards with an optional application identifier
.RE
.RE
.PP
\fBframework \fR\fB\fIname\fR\fR\fB { \fR\fB\fIblock_contents\fR\fR\fB } \fR
.RS 4
Internal configuration options where
\fIname\fR
is one of:
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
pkcs15: See
the section called \(lqConfiguration of PKCS#15 Framework\(rq
.RE
.sp
.RE
.PP
\fBpkcs11 { \fR\fB\fIblock_contents\fR\fR\fB } \fR
.RS 4
Parameters for the OpenSC PKCS11 module\&.
.sp
For details see
the section called \(lqConfiguration of PKCS#11\(rq\&.
.RE
.SS "Configuration of Smart Card Reader Driver"
.sp
.it 1 an-trap
.nr an-no-space-flag 1
.nr an-break-flag 1
.br
.ps +1
\fBConfiguration Options for all Reader Drivers\fR
.RS 4
.PP
\fBmax_send_size = \fR\fB\fInum\fR\fR\fB;\fR \fBmax_recv_size = \fR\fB\fInum\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Limit command and response sizes (Default:
\fBmax_send_size\fR
=
255,
\fBmax_recv_size\fR
=
256) \&. Some Readers don\*(Aqt propagate their transceive capabilities correctly\&. max_send_size and max_recv_size allow setting the limits manually, for example to enable extended length capabilities\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBenable_escape \fR\fB\fIbool\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Detect reader capabilities with escape commands (wrapped APDUs with CLA=0xFF as defined by PC/SC pt\&. 3 and BSI TR\-03119, e\&.g\&. for getting the UID, escaped PIN commands and the reader\*(Aqs firmware version, Default:
false)
.RE
.RE
.sp
.it 1 an-trap
.nr an-no-space-flag 1
.nr an-break-flag 1
.br
.ps +1
\fBConfiguration of CT-API Readers\fR
.RS 4
.PP
\fBmodule \fR\fB\fIfilename\fR\fR\fB { ports = \fR\fB\fInums\fR\fR\fB; } \fR
.RS 4
Load the specified CT\-API module with the specified number of ports\&.
.RE
.RE
.sp
.it 1 an-trap
.nr an-no-space-flag 1
.nr an-break-flag 1
.br
.ps +1
\fBConfiguration of PC/SC Readers\fR
.RS 4
.PP
\fBconnect_exclusive = \fR\fB\fIbool\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Connect to reader in exclusive mode (Default:
false)? This option has no effect in Windows\*(Aq minidriver\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBdisconnect_action = \fR\fB\fIaction\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
What to do when disconnecting from a card (SCardDisconnect)\&. Valid values are
leave,
reset,
unpower
(Default:
leave)\&. This option has no effect in Windows\*(Aq minidriver\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBtransaction_end_action = \fR\fB\fIaction\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
What to do at the end of a transaction (SCardEndTransaction)\&. Valid values are
leave,
reset,
unpower
(Default:
leave)\&. This option has no effect in Windows\*(Aq minidriver\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBreconnect_action = \fR\fB\fIaction\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
What to do when reconnection to a card (SCardReconnect)\&. Valid values are
leave,
reset,
unpower
(Default:
leave)\&. This option has no effect in Windows\*(Aq minidriver\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBenable_pinpad = \fR\fB\fIbool\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Enable pinpad if detected (PC/SC v2\&.0\&.2 Part 10, Default:
true)
.RE
.PP
\fBfixed_pinlength = \fR\fB\fInum\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Some pinpad readers can only handle one exact length of the PIN\&.
\fBfixed_pinlength\fR
sets this value so that OpenSC expands the padding to this length (Default:
0, i\&.e\&. not fixed)\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBprovider_library = \fR\fB\fIfilename\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Use specific PC/SC provider (Default:
libpcsclite\&.so\&.1)\&.
.RE
.RE
.sp
.it 1 an-trap
.nr an-no-space-flag 1
.nr an-break-flag 1
.br
.ps +1
\fBConfiguration of OpenCT Readers\fR
.RS 4
.PP
\fBreaders = \fR\fB\fInum\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Virtual readers to allocate (Default:
2)\&.
.RE
.RE
.SS "Configuration Options for MyEID Card"
.PP
\fBdisable_hw_pkcs1_padding = \fR\fB\fIbool\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
The MyEID card can internally encapsulate the data (hash code) into a DigestInfo ASN\&.1 structure according to the selected hash algorithm (currently only for SHA1)\&. DigestInfo is padded to RSA key modulus length according to PKCS#1 v1\&.5, block type 01h\&. Size of the DigestInfo must not exceed 40% of the RSA key modulus length\&. If this limit is unsatisfactory (for example someone needs RSA 1024 with SHA512), the user can disable this feature\&. In this case, the card driver will do everything necessary before sending the data (hash code) to the card\&.
.sp
PKCS#1 v1\&.5 padding in HW can be globally disabled by option
disable_hw_pkcs1_padding\&. When the global option is used to disable padding, the padding will be disabled even though the MyEID\-specific option does not turn it off\&.
.RE
.SS "Configuration Options for German ID Card"
.PP
\fBcan = \fR\fB\fIvalue\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
German ID card requires the CAN to be verified before QES PIN\&. This, however, is not part of the PKCS#15 profile of the card\&. So for verifying the QES PIN we actually need both\&. The CAN may be given here\&. If the CAN is not given here, it will be prompted on the command line or on the reader (depending on the reader\*(Aqs capabilities)\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBst_dv_certificate = \fR\fB\fIfilename\fR\fR\fB;\fR \fBst_certificate = \fR\fB\fIfilename\fR\fR\fB;\fR \fBst_key = \fR\fB\fIfilename\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
QES is only possible with a Comfort Reader (CAT\-K), which holds a cryptographic key to authenticate itself as signature terminal (ST)\&. We usually will use the reader\*(Aqs capability to sign the data\&. However, during development you may specify soft certificates and keys for a ST\&.
.sp
An example PKI can be found in the example data for the
\m[blue]\fBGerman ID card emulator\fR\m[]\&\s-2\u[1]\d\s+2
.RE
.SS "Configuration Options for DNIe"
.PP
\fBuser_consent_enabled = \fR\fB\fIbool\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Configure the warning message when performing a signature operation with the DNIe\&. Only used if compiled with
\fB\-\-enable\-dnie\-ui\fR
.RE
.PP
\fBuser_consent_app = \fR\fB\fIfilename\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Specify the pinentry application to use if warning is configured to be displayed using pinentry (Default:
/usr/bin/pinentry)\&. Only used if compiled with
\fB\-\-enable\-dnie\-ui\fR
.RE
.SS "Configuration Options for Polish eID Card"
.PP
\fBcan = \fR\fB\fIvalue\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
CAN (Card Access Number \(en 6 digit number printed on the right bottom corner of the front side of the document) is required to establish connection with the card\&. It might be overwritten by
EDO_CAN
environment variable\&. Currently, it is not possible to set it in any other way\&.
.RE
.SS "Configuration Options for Slovenian eID Card"
.PP
\fBcan = \fR\fB\fIvalue\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
CAN (Card Access Number \(en 6 digit number printed on the right bottom corner of the front side of the document) is required to establish connection with the card\&. It might be overwritten by
EOI_CAN
environment variable\&. As CAN is also stored on the card (in encrypted form) it can be used to automatically establish secure connection, but only if the card is accessed over the contact interface\&.
.RE
.SS "Configuration Options for D\-Trust Signature Cards"
.PP
\fBcan = \fR\fB\fIvalue\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
CAN (Card Access Number \(en 6 digit number printed on the front side of the card) is required to establish connection with the card\&. It might be overwritten by
DTRUST_CAN
environment variable\&. If not specified here, the CAN will be read from a card specific cache, prompted on the card readers PIN pad or prompted interactively in the following order\&.
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04' 1.\h'+01'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP "  1." 4.2
.\}
Environment variable
DTRUST_CAN
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04' 2.\h'+01'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP "  2." 4.2
.\}
This configuration file option
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04' 3.\h'+01'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP "  3." 4.2
.\}
PKCS#15 card\-specific cache
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04' 4.\h'+01'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP "  4." 4.2
.\}
Pin pad of a PACE\-capable card reader
.RE
.RE
.PP
\fBcan_use_cache = \fR\fB\fIbool\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Cache the CAN number of a card once it was provided by the user in the directory
file_cache_dir\&. The cached CAN is used later to avoid interactively prompting for the CAN\&. This feature is enabled by default\&.
.RE
.SS "Configuration Options for PIV Card"
.SS "Configuration based on ATR"
.PP
.PP
\fBatrmask = \fR\fB\fIhexstring\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
The mask is logically AND\*(Aqd with an card ATR prior to comparison with the ATR reference value above\&. Using this mask allows identifying and configuring multiple ATRs as the same card model\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBdriver = \fR\fB\fIname\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
When enabled, overrides all possible settings from the card drivers built\-in card configuration list\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBname = \fR\fB\fIname\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Set card name for card drivers that allows it\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBtype = \fR\fB\fInum\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Allows setting the exact type of the card internally used by the card driver\&. Allowed values can be found in the source code of
cards\&.h\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBflags = \fR\fB\fIvalue\fR...\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Card flags as an hex value\&. Multiple values are OR\*(Aqd together\&. Depending on card driver, this allows fine\-tuning the capabilities in the card driver for your card\&.
.sp
Optionally, some known parameters can be specified as strings:
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
rng: On\-board random number source
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
keep_alive: Request the card driver to send a "keep alive" command before each transaction to make sure that the required applet is still selected\&.
.RE
.sp
.RE
.PP
\fBpkcs15emu = \fR\fB\fIname\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
When using PKCS#15 emulation, force the emulation driver for specific cards\&. Required for external drivers, but can be used with built\-in drivers, too\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBforce_protocol = \fR\fB\fIvalue\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Force protocol selection for specific cards\&. Known parameters:
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
t0
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
t1
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
raw
.RE
.sp
.RE
.PP
\fBread_only = \fR\fB\fIbool\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Mark card as read/only card in PKCS#11/Minidriver/BaseCSP interface (Default:
false)\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBmd_supports_X509_enrollment = \fR\fB\fIbool\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Indicate X509 enrollment support at Minidriver/BaseCSP interface (Default:
false)\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBmd_guid_as_id = \fR\fB\fIbool\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Use the GUID generated for the key as id in the PKCS#15 structure (Default:
false, i\&.e\&. auto generated)
.RE
.PP
\fBmd_guid_as_label = \fR\fB\fIbool\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Use the GUID generated for the key as label in the PKCS#15 structure (Default:
false, i\&.e\&. no label set)\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBmd_supports_container_key_gen = \fR\fB\fIbool\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Card allows generating key pairs on the card (Default:
false)\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBmd_supports_container_key_import = \fR\fB\fIbool\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Card allows importing private keys (Default:
false)\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBmd_pinpad_dlg_title = \fR\fB\fIvalue\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Window title of the PIN pad dialog (Default:
"Windows Security")\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBmd_pinpad_dlg_icon = \fR\fB\fIfilename\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Filename of the icon for the PIN pad dialog; use
""
for no icon (Default: Built\-in smart card icon)\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBmd_pinpad_dlg_main = \fR\fB\fIvalue\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Main instruction of the PIN pad dialog (Default:
"OpenSC Smart Card Provider")\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBmd_pinpad_dlg_content_user = \fR\fB\fIvalue\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Content of the PIN pad dialog for role "user" (Default:
"Please enter your PIN on the PIN pad\&.")\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBmd_pinpad_dlg_content_user_sign = \fR\fB\fIvalue\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Content of the PIN pad dialog for role "user+signature" (Default:
"Please enter your digital signature PIN on the PIN pad\&.")\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBmd_pinpad_dlg_content_admin = \fR\fB\fIvalue\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Content of the PIN pad dialog for role "admin" (Default:
"Please enter your PIN to unblock the user PIN on the PIN pad\&.")
.RE
.PP
\fBmd_pinpad_dlg_expanded = \fR\fB\fIvalue\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Expanded information of the PIN pad dialog (Default:
"This window will be closed automatically after the PIN has been submitted on the PIN pad (timeout typically after 30 seconds)\&.")
.RE
.PP
\fBmd_pinpad_dlg_enable_cancel = \fR\fB\fIbool\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Allow the user to cancel the PIN pad dialog (Default:
false)\&. If this value is set to
true, the user needs to click "OK" to start the PIN verification on the PIN pad\&. The user can choose the default behavior by enabling or disabling the checkbox of the dialog\&. The setting is saved by the program\*(Aqs full path (\fIprogram_path\fR) that uses OpenSC\&.
.sp
The registry key
HKCU\eSoftware\eOpenSC Project\eOpenSC\emd_pinpad_dlg_enable_cancel\e\fIprogram_path\fR
overwrites this setting with a
DWORD
set to either
1
(enabled) or
0
(disabled)\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBmd_pinpad_dlg_timeout = \fR\fB\fInum\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Time in seconds for the progress bar of the PIN pad dialog to tick\&.
0
removes the progress bar (Default:
30)\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBnotify_card_inserted = \fR\fB\fIvalue\fR\fR\fB;\fR \fBnotify_card_inserted_text = \fR\fB\fIvalue\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Notification title and text when card was inserted (Default:
"Smart card detected", ATR of the card)\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBnotify_card_removed = \fR\fB\fIvalue\fR\fR\fB;\fR \fBnotify_card_removed_text = \fR\fB\fIvalue\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Notification title and text when card was removed (Default:
"Smart card removed", name of smart card reader)\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBnotify_pin_good = \fR\fB\fIvalue\fR\fR\fB;\fR \fBnotify_pin_good_text = \fR\fB\fIvalue\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Notification title and text when PIN was verified (Default:
"PIN verified",
"Smart card is unlocked")\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBnotify_pin_bad = \fR\fB\fIvalue\fR\fR\fB;\fR \fBnotify_pin_bad_text = \fR\fB\fIvalue\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Notification title and text when PIN was wrong (Default:
"PIN not verified",
"Smart card is locked")\&.
.RE
.SS "Configuration of PKCS#15 Framework"
.PP
\fBuse_file_caching = \fR\fB\fIvalue\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Whether to cache the card\*(Aqs files (e\&.g\&. certificates) on disk in
\fBfile_cache_dir\fR\&. Possible parameters:
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
yes: Cache all files (public and private)\&.
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
public: Cache only public files\&.
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
no: File caching disabled\&.
.RE
.sp
(Default:
public
for the following card drivers
atrust\-acos
(deactivated driver),
belpic,
cac1,
cac,
coolkey,
dnie,
edo,
esteid2018,
esteid2025,
flex
(deactivated driver),
cyberflex
(deactivated driver),
gemsafeV1,
idprime,
itacns,
jpki,
MaskTech,
mcrd
(deactivated driver),
npa,
nqapplet,
tcos,
dtrust
and otherwise
no)\&.
.sp
If caching is done by a system process, the cached files may be placed inaccessible from the user account\&. Use a globally readable and writable location if you wish to share the cached information\&. Note that the cached files may contain personal data such as name and mail address\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBfile_cache_dir = \fR\fB\fIfilename\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Where to cache the card\*(Aqs files\&. The default values are:
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
\fB$XDG_CACHE_HOME\fR/opensc/
(If
\fB$XDG_CACHE_HOME\fR
is defined)
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
\fB$HOME\fR/\&.cache/opensc/
(Unix)
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
\fB$USERPROFILE\fR\e\&.eid\-cache\e
(Windows)
.RE
.sp
If caching is done by a system process, the cached files may be placed inaccessible from a user account\&. Use a globally readable and writable location if you wish to share the cached information\&. Note that the cached files may contain personal data such as name and mail address\&.
.sp
The PIV\-II card driver supports the history object\*(Aqs list of retired keys and certificates if they are readable in the file cache directory\&. If the specified object\*(Aqs URL is
"http://"\fIDNS name\fR"/"\fIASCII\-HEX OffCardKeyHistoryFile\fR, then the searches for the file name
\fIOffCardKeyHistoryFile\fR
in the cache directory\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBuse_pin_caching = \fR\fB\fIbool\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Use PIN caching (Default:
true)?
.RE
.PP
\fBpin_cache_counter = \fR\fB\fInum\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
How many times to use a PIN from cache before re\-authenticating it (Default:
10)?
.RE
.PP
\fBpin_cache_ignore_user_consent = \fR\fB\fIbool\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Older PKCS#11 applications not supporting
CKA_ALWAYS_AUTHENTICATE
may need to set this to get signatures to work with some cards (Default:
false)\&.
.sp
It is recommended to enable also PIN caching using
use_pin_caching
option for OpenSC to be able to provide PIN for the card when needed\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBpin_protected_certificate = \fR\fB\fIvalue\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
How to handle a PIN\-protected certificate\&. Known parameters:
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
protect: The certificate stays PIN\-protected\&.
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
declassify: Allow reading the certificate without enforcing verification of the PIN\&.
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
ignore: Ignore PIN\-protected certificates\&.
.RE
.sp
(Default:
protect\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBenable_pkcs15_emulation = \fR\fB\fIbool\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Enable pkcs15 emulation (Default:
true)\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBtry_emulation_first = \fR\fB\fIbool\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Prefer pkcs15 emulation code before the normal pkcs15 processing (Default:
no)\&. Some cards work in emu\-only mode, and do not depend on this option\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBenable_builtin_emulation = \fR\fB\fIbool\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Enable builtin emulators (Default:
true)\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBbuiltin_emulators = \fR\fB\fIemulators\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
List of the builtin pkcs15 emulators to test (Default:
internal)
.sp
Special value of
internal
will try all not disabled builtin pkcs15 emulators\&.
.sp
Special value of
old
will try all disabled pkcs15 emulators\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBpkcs11_enable_InitToken = \fR\fB\fIbool\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Enable initialization and card recognition (Default:
false)\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBemulate \fR\fB\fIname\fR\fR\fB { \fR\fB\fIblock_contents\fR\fR\fB } \fR
.RS 4
Configuration options for a PKCS#15 emulator where
\fIname\fR
is a short name for an external card driver\&.
.PP
\fBmodule = \fR\fB\fIfilename\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
For pkcs15 emulators loaded from an external shared library/DLL, you need to specify the path name of the module and customize the card_atr example above correctly\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBfunction = \fR\fB\fIname\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Get the init function name of the emulator (Default:
sc_pkcs15_init_func_ex)
.RE
.RE
.PP
\fBapplication \fR\fB\fIhexstring\fR\fR\fB { \fR\fB\fIblock_contents\fR\fR\fB } \fR
.RS 4
Configuration of the on\-card\-application where
\fIhexstring\fR
is the application identifier (AID)\&.
.PP
\fBtype = \fR\fB\fIname\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Type of application where
\fIname\fR
is one of:
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
generic
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
protected
.RE
.sp
Used to distinguish the common access application and application for which authentication to perform some operation cannot be obtained with the common procedures (ex\&. object creation protected by secure messaging)\&. Used by PKCS#11 module configured to expose restricted number of slots\&. (for ex\&. configured to expose only User PIN slot, User and Sign PINs slots, \&.\&.\&.)
.RE
.PP
\fBmodel = \fR\fB\fIname\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
.RE
.PP
\fBdisable = \fR\fB\fIbool\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Do not expose application in PKCS#15 framework (Default:
false)
.RE
.PP
\fBuser_pin = \fR\fB\fIname\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Name of the User PIN object that will be used as the main PIN\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBsign_pin = \fR\fB\fIname\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Name of the PIN object that will be used for signing\&.
.RE
.RE
.SS "Configuration of PKCS#11"
.PP
\fBmax_virtual_slots = \fR\fB\fInum\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Maximum Number of virtual slots (Default:
16)\&. If there are more slots than defined here, the remaining slots will be hidden from PKCS#11\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBslots_per_card = \fR\fB\fInum\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Maximum number of PIN slots per smart card (Default:
4)\&. If the card has fewer PINs than defined here, the remaining number of slots will be empty\&. For Firefox, Chrome and Chromium, the
\fBslots_per_card\fR
is set to
1, to avoid prompting for unrelated PINs\&. Typically, this effectively disables signature PINs and keys\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBlock_login = \fR\fB\fIbool\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
By default, the OpenSC PKCS#11 module will not lock your card once you authenticate to the card via
C_Login
(Default:
false)\&. Thus the other users or other applications is not prevented from connecting to the card and perform crypto operations (which may be possible because you have already authenticated with the card)\&. This setting is not very secure\&.
.sp
Also, if your card is not locked, you can enconter problems due to limitation of the OpenSC framework, that still is not thoroughly tested in the multi threads environment\&.
.sp
Your settings will be more secure if you choose to lock your card\&. Nevertheless this behavior is a known violation of PKCS#11 specification\&. Now once one application has started using your card with
C_Login, no other application can use it, until the first is done and calls
C_Logout
or
C_Finalize\&. In the case of many PKCS#11 application this does not happen until you exit the application\&.
.sp
Thus it is impossible to use several smart card aware applications at the same time, e\&.g\&. you cannot run both
Firefox
and
Thunderbird
at the same time, if both are configured to use your smart card\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBatomic = \fR\fB\fIbool\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
By default, interacting with the OpenSC PKCS#11 module may change the state of the token, e\&.g\&. whether a user is logged in or not (Default:
false)\&.
.sp
Thus other users or other applications may change or use the state of the token unknowingly\&. Other applications may create signatures abusing an existing login or they may logout unnoticed\&.
.sp
With this setting enabled the login state of the token is tracked and cached (including the PIN)\&. Every transaction is preceded by restoring the login state\&. After every transaction a logout is performed\&. This setting by default also enables
\fBlock_login\fR
to disable access for other applications during the atomic transactions\&.
.sp
Please note that any PIN\-pad should be disabled (see
\fBenable_pinpad\fR), because the user would have to input his PIN for every transaction\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBinit_sloppy = \fR\fB\fIbool\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
With this setting disabled, the OpenSC PKCS#11 module will initialize the slots available when the application calls
C_GetSlotList\&. With this setting enabled, the slots will also get initialized when
C_GetSlotInfo
is called (Default:
true)\&.
.sp
This setting is a workaround for
Java
which does not call
C_GetSlotList
when configured with a static
slot
instead of
slotListIndex\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBuser_pin_unblock_style = \fR\fB\fImode\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
User PIN unblock style
\fImode\fR
is one of:
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
none
(Default): PIN unblock is not possible with PKCS#11 API
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
set_pin_in_unlogged_session:
C_SetPIN
in unlogged session: PUK is passed as the
OldPin
argument of the
C_SetPIN
call\&.
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
set_pin_in_specific_context:
C_SetPIN
in the
CKU_SPECIFIC_CONTEXT
logged session: PUK is passed as the
OldPin
argument of the
C_SetPIN
call\&.
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
init_pin_in_so_session:
C_InitPIN
in
CKU_SO
logged session: User PIN \*(AqUNBLOCK\*(Aq is protected by SOPIN\&. (PUK == SOPIN)\&.
.RE
.sp
.RE
.PP
\fBcreate_puk_slot = \fR\fB\fIbool\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Create slot for unblocking PIN with PUK (Default:
false)\&. This way PKCS#11 API can be used to login with PUK and change a PIN\&. May cause problems with some applications like
Firefox
and
Thunderbird\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBcreate_slots_for_pins = \fR\fB\fImode\fR...\fR\fB;\fR
.RS 4
Symbolic names of PINs for which slots are created where
\fImode\fR
is a list of:
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
all
(Default): All non\-SO\-PIN, non\-unblocking PINs
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
user: The first global or first local PIN
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.sp -1
.IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
sign: The second PIN (first local, second global or second local)
.RE
.sp
Card can contain more then one PINs or more then one on\-card application with its own PINs\&. Normally, to access all of them with the PKCS#11 API a slot has to be created for all of them\&. Many slots could be annoying for some of widely used application, like FireFox\&. This configuration parameter allows to select the PIN(s) for which PKCS#11 slot will be created\&.
.sp
Only PINs initialised, non\-SO\-PIN, non\-unblocking are associated with symbolic name\&.
.sp
For the module to simulate the opensc\-onepin module behavior the following option
\fBcreate_slots_for_pins = "user";\fR
.RE
.SH "محیط (ENVIRONMENT)"
.PP
\fBOPENSC_CONF\fR
.RS 4
Filename for a user defined configuration file
.sp
If this environment variable is not found on Windows, the registry key
Software\eOpenSC Project\eOpenSC\eConfigFile
is checked\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBOPENSC_DEBUG\fR
.RS 4
See
\fBdebug = \fR\fB\fInum\fR\fR\fB;\fR
.RE
.PP
\fBOPENSC_DRIVER\fR
.RS 4
See
\fBcard_drivers = \fR\fB\fIname\fR...\fR\fB;\fR
.RE
.PP
\fBCARDMOD_LOW_LEVEL_DEBUG\fR
.RS 4
Write minidriver debug information to
C:\etmp\emd\&.log, if set to
1\&.
.sp
If this environment variable is not found on Windows, the registry key
Software\eOpenSC Project\eOpenSC\eMiniDriverDebug
is checked\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBPIV_EXT_AUTH_KEY\fR, \fBPIV_9A_KEY\fR, \fBPIV_9C_KEY\fR, \fBPIV_9D_KEY\fR, \fBPIV_9E_KEY\fR
.RS 4
PIV configuration during initialization with
piv\-tool\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBPIV_USE_SM\fR, \fBPIV_PAIRING_CODE\fR
.RS 4
PIV configuration during initialization See Configuration Options for PIV Card\&.
.RE
.SH "فایل‌ها (FILES)"
.PP
/etc/opensc\&.conf
.RS 4
System\-wide configuration file
.RE
.PP
/usr/share/doc/opensc/opensc\&.conf
.RS 4
Extended example configuration file
.RE
